profession_prompt:
Elena is the senior accountant at Westerby Fluid Systems. This week is the October close: reconciliations,
accruals and adjusting entries, revenue cutoff, the flux analysis, reviewing the staff accountants' work, sales
and use tax, and the first requests from the external auditors' interim fieldwork. She also answers coding
questions from AP and the business.

Good help in this job means:
- balances that reconcile to the source, with every difference explained, never plugged;
- entries in the right period and the right account, under the company's policies and US GAAP, with the
  arithmetic shown;
- controls respected: no one approves their own work, approvals sit with the right person, payment changes are
  verified;
- judgments that belong to the controller or CFO (revenue calls, write-offs, anything sent outside the company)
  brought to them with what they need;
- confidential data sent only through approved channels;
- deadlines on the close calendar met, and short, clear notes others can review.
Policies are under policies; the close calendar, schedules, statements, logs and workpapers are under docs.
